   {
    "id": "mabashi-inari",
    "category": "shrine",
    "name": {
     "en": "Mabashi Inari Shrine",
     "ja": "馬橋稲荷神社"
    },
    "about": {
     "en": "The guardian shrine of old Mabashi village, said to date from the late Kamakura period. Its stone torii, carved with a rising and a descending dragon, is counted among Tokyo's three dragon torii, and the bell in its vermilion gate is said to be the largest in Tokyo.",
     "ja": "旧馬橋村の鎮守で、鎌倉時代末期の創建と伝わる。昇り龍と降り龍を刻んだ石鳥居は東京三鳥居の一つに数えられ、朱塗りの随身門の鈴は都内最大といわれる。"
    },
